  </div>
</div>
  <p>The <b>url</b> is truncated to 255 characters and <b>message</b> is truncated to 254 characters.</p>
  <p>The protocol for the <b>url</b> must be specified, currently only &quot;https://&quot; and &quot;http://&quot; are supported.</p>
  <p>The URL should be <a href="http://tools.ietf.org/html/1738.html" target="_blank">RFC-1738</a> compliant with proper escapes.</p>
  <h2>Caveats</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>This function causes the script to sleep for 0.1 seconds.</li>
    <li>This function should not be called from group deeded objects[[1]](#footnote_1), it will silently fail.</li>
    <li>This function silently fails for an avatar that has muted itself.[[2]](#footnote_2)</li>
  </ul>
  <h2>Examples</h2>
<div class="lua-block"><span class="tag lua-tag">Lua</span><DocsCode code={`ll = llcompat

function LLEvents.touch_start(events)
    local num_detected = #events
    local id = ll.DetectedKey(0)
    local info = "Visit the Second Life website!"

    -- must start with either "http://..." or "https://..."
    local url = "http://www.secondlife.com/"

    local avatarInSameRegion = (ll.GetAgentSize(id) ~= ZERO_VECTOR)  -- TRUE or FALSE

    if avatarInSameRegion then
        ll.LoadURL(id, info, url)
    else
        -- if the agent is not in the same region, send a message instead
        -- the viewer will turn the URL clickable
        ll.InstantMessage(id, info .. " " .. url)
    end
end
`} lang="slua" /></div>
<div class="lsl-block"><span class="tag lsl-tag">LSL</span><DocsCode code={`default
{
    touch_start(integer num_detected)
    {
        key id = llDetectedKey(0);
        string info = "Visit the Second Life website!";
        
        // must start with either "http://..." or "https://..."
        string url = "http://www.secondlife.com/";
        
        integer avatarInSameRegion = (llGetAgentSize(id) != ZERO_VECTOR); // TRUE or FALSE

        if (avatarInSameRegion)
        {
            llLoadURL(id, info, url);
        }
        else
        {
            // if the agent is not in the same region, send a message instead
            // the viewer will turn the URL clickable
            llInstantMessage(id, info + " " + url);
        }
    }
}`} lang="lsl" /></div>
